Agent Deck v1.14.0
Terminal session manager for AI coding agents

Usage: agent-deck [-p profile] [-g group] [--select id|title] [command]

Global Options:
  -p, --profile <name>   Use specific profile (default: 'default')
  -g, --group <name>     Launch TUI scoped to a specific group
  --select <id|title>    Launch TUI with cursor on a specific session (all groups stay visible)

Commands:
  (none)           Start the TUI
  add <path>       Add a new session
  launch [path]    Add, start, and optionally send a message in one step
  try <name>       Quick experiment (create/find dated folder + session)
  list, ls         List all sessions
  remove, rm       Remove a session
  rename, mv       Rename a session
  status           Show session status summary
  session          Manage session lifecycle
  fleet            Detect and recover from a fleet-wide session death
  mcp              Manage MCP servers
  skill            Manage project skills
  codex-hooks      Manage Codex notify hook integration
  gemini-hooks     Manage Gemini hook integration
  hermes-hooks     Manage Hermes Agent hook integration
  cursor-hooks     Manage Cursor Agent CLI hook integration
  deepseek         Inspect the DeepSeek Harness (dsh) integration
  group            Manage groups
  worktree, wt     Manage git worktrees
  web              Start TUI with web UI server running alongside
  remote           Manage remote agent-deck instances
  conductor        Manage conductor meta-agent orchestration
  telegram-doctor  Audit channel-owning sessions for telegram drops (#1138)
  profile          Manage profiles
  update           Check for and install updates
  debug-dump       Dump debug ring buffer to file for sharing
  migrate-paths    Copy legacy ~/.agent-deck files into XDG paths
  uninstall        Uninstall Agent Deck
  version          Show version
  help             Show this help

Session Commands:
  session start <id>        Start a session's tmux process
  session stop <id>         Stop session process
  session restart <id>      Restart session (reload MCPs)
  session fork <id>         Fork Claude or Pi session with context
  session attach <id>       Attach to session interactively
  session show [id]         Show session details

Fleet Recovery Commands:
  fleet status              Report sessions whose panes are gone (read-only)
  fleet recover             Plan a sequential recovery sweep (add --yes to run it)

MCP Commands:
  mcp list                  List available MCPs from config.toml
  mcp attached [id]         Show MCPs attached to a session
  mcp attach <id> <mcp>     Attach MCP to session
  mcp detach <id> <mcp>     Detach MCP from session

Skill Commands:
  skill list                List discoverable skills
  skill attached [id]       Show skills attached to a session
  skill attach <id> <name>  Attach skill to session project
  skill detach <id> <name>  Detach skill from session project
  skill source list         List global skill sources

Codex Hook Commands:
  codex-hooks install       Install or upgrade Codex notify hook
  codex-hooks uninstall     Remove Codex notify hook
  codex-hooks status        Show Codex hook install status
  gemini-hooks install      Install Gemini hooks
  gemini-hooks uninstall    Remove Gemini hooks
  gemini-hooks status       Show Gemini hooks install status
  hermes-hooks install      Install Hermes Agent hooks
  hermes-hooks uninstall    Remove Hermes Agent hooks
  hermes-hooks status       Show Hermes hooks install status
  cursor-hooks install      Install Cursor hooks
  cursor-hooks uninstall    Remove Cursor hooks
  cursor-hooks status       Show Cursor hooks install status
  deepseek status           Show resolved dsh binary, DSH_HOME, profile
  deepseek profiles         List profiles under $DSH_HOME/profiles
  deepseek sessions [path]  List dsh sessions recorded for a workspace

Group Commands:
  group list                List all groups
  group create <name>       Create a new group
  group delete <name>       Delete a group
  group move <id> <group>   Move session to group

Conductor Commands:
  conductor setup           Set up conductor (Telegram bridge + sessions)
  conductor teardown        Stop conductor and remove bridge daemon
  conductor status          Show conductor health across profiles
  conductor list            List configured conductors

Remote Commands:
  remote add <name> <user@host>             Register a remote agent-deck instance
