149-
150-### Shift+Enter Submits Instead of Inserting a Newline (Kitty)
151-
152-In **kitty**, Shift+Enter (and other modified keys) may submit immediately
153-inside agent-deck even though they insert a newline when the agent runs
154:natively. This is a kitty-specific quirk: tmux negotiates extended keys with
155-the outer terminal using xterm's *modifyOtherKeys* protocol, which kitty does
156-not implement (kitty only speaks its own CSI-u keyboard protocol). So kitty
157-keeps sending a bare carriage return and the agent submits.
158-
159:agent-deck already sets `extended-keys-format csi-u` on its tmux sessions so
160-that, *once the terminal sends a distinct Shift+Enter*, it reaches the agent in
161-the form Claude Code understands. The remaining piece must be set in kitty
162-itself — make kitty emit the CSI-u Shift+Enter unconditionally:
163-
164-```conf
165-# ~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf
166-map shift+enter send_text all \x1b[13;2u
167-```
168-
169-Reload kitty's config (`Ctrl+Shift+F5`) and Shift+Enter will insert a newline,
170-both natively and inside agent-deck. iTerm2, Ghostty, WezTerm and xterm honor
171-modifyOtherKeys and do not need this mapping.
--
